Fixed: MappingFE::transform_real_to_unit_cell() now starts the Newton
iteration from the inverse of the affine map through the vertices for
simplices and from the barycenter of the reference cell otherwise, instead of
the origin of the reference cell, and halves the Newton step until the
residual decreases. If the iteration does not converge from the affine map or
converges to a point outside of the reference cell, it is restarted from the
barycenter. For a point outside of the cell, the result closest to the
reference cell is returned. This improves robustness for curved cells of all
types.
The iteration no longer needs the second derivatives of the shape functions,
which are not implemented for wedges and pyramids, such that the function now
also works for these cells.
